      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like you are reading either 8 bytes or 16 bytes here. Which means reading beyond the end of the slice if the remainder is 1-7 or 9-15 bytes long. I don\u0027t think that is safe. The input isn\u0027t necessarily aligned to 8 bytes so a read beyond the end of the slice might cross a page boundary and trigger a segmentation fault.\n\nProbably better to stick to loading one byte at a time like the original code does.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "38b1f8a3c47c25cc3487db5d822761061a6d7819",
